dura mater.d:
The tough, fibrous membrane, which lines the cavity of
   the skull and spinal column, and surrounds the brain and spinal cord;
   -- frequently abbreviated to dura.

durometer.d:
n. An instrument for measuring the degree of hardness;
   especially, an instrument for testing the relative hardness of steel
   rails and the like.

edulcorator.d:
n. A contrivance used to supply small quantities of
   sweetened liquid, water, etc., to any mixture, or to test tubes, etc.;
   a dropping bottle.

effulge.d:
v. t. To cause to shine with abundance of light; to radiate;
   to beam.
v. i. To shine forth; to beam.
